{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TotallyGeodesicFaces","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TotallyGeodesicFaces","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GeodesicFaceH3","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Euclidean.Inversion.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphere_isTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphere_isTotallyGeodesic","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L213-L259","doc":"**The corpus hemisphere is totally geodesic** (conditional on the geodesic-\nuniqueness wall `HypMinimizerUnique`), for any radius `R > 0` — the exact\nhemispherical face the ideal tetrahedron intersects.\n\nDERIVED from the boundary inversion in the sphere of radius `R` centred at the\norigin (`c = 0`, which lies on `∂H³`): its fixed set is that Euclidean sphere, and\na minimiser between two `H³` points stays in `H³` (`z > 0`), so it stays in the\nhemisphere `sphere ∩ {z > 0}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zero_apply_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zero_apply_two","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L210-L211","doc":"The origin has vanishing height coordinate (it is a boundary centre). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dist_zero_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dist_zero_sq","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L201-L208","doc":"`dist p 0 = ‖p‖`, and `‖p‖² = ∑ (p i)²` on the Euclidean carrier — the bridge\nbetween the inversion's `dist`-language and the corpus sphere equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.mem_hemisphereE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.mem_hemisphereE","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L198-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereE","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L194-L196","doc":"The corpus hemisphere, transported to `E` by `EuclideanSpace.equiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlane_isTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlane_isTotallyGeodesic","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L175-L190","doc":"**The corpus vertical plane is totally geodesic** (conditional on the\ngeodesic-uniqueness wall `HypMinimizerUnique`), for ANY unit base normal `n` and\nANY offset `d` — the exact vertical faces the ideal tetrahedron intersects.\n\nDERIVED from the general reflection `vReflect n d`'s isometry via\n`fixedSet_isTotallyGeodesic`; it strictly generalises the merged\n`verticalPlaneFix_isTotallyGeodesic` (the `n = (1,0), d = 0` instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.mem_verticalPlaneE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.mem_verticalPlaneE","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L172-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneE","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L167-L170","doc":"The corpus vertical plane, transported to the Euclidean carrier `E` by the\n(coordinate-identity) equivalence `EuclideanSpace.equiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vReflect_fixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vReflect_fixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L149-L163","doc":"**Fixed-set characterisation.**  For a unit normal, `vReflect n d` fixes `p`\niff `p` lies on the corpus vertical plane `p₀·n.1 + p₁·n.2 = d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vReflect_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vReflect_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L140-L147","doc":"The general vertical reflection is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneReflectionIsom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneReflectionIsom","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L106-L138","doc":"**The conformal height-scaling data of the general vertical reflection**\n(`lam ≡ 1`).  Its Fréchet derivative is the Householder linear map (norm-preserving,\nfactor `1`), and it fixes the height coordinate (factor `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.householder_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.householder_norm","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L93-L104","doc":"Householder norm preservation: `‖v − 2⟪ñ,v⟫·ñ‖ = ‖v‖` for a unit `ñ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vReflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vReflect","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L87-L91","doc":"**The general vertical-plane reflection.**  Householder reflection across\n`{p | ⟪ñ, p⟫ = d}`.  At `n = (1,0), d = 0` this is the merged `verticalReflection`\n(reflection across `{x = 0}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L73-L78","doc":"For a unit base normal, the normal is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner_verticalPlaneNormal_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner_verticalPlaneNormal_self","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L67-L71","doc":"For a unit base normal, the vertical-plane normal is a unit inner-product\nvector: `⟪ñ, ñ⟫ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal_apply_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal_apply_two","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The vertical-plane normal has vanishing height coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner_verticalPlaneNormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner_verticalPlaneNormal","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TotallyGeodesicFaces.lean#L54-L61","doc":"The inner product with the vertical-plane normal is the base-line functional\n`n.1·p₀ + n.2·p₁` (the `z`-component of the normal is `0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}